{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-dm.7.1:000025:note_appended:bob-cli-dm.7.1.3:5717845b866ebcb211fb43c6fb53eada74dd759d23ba247a2af5a1b1ac5ba8e1","timestamp":"2026-10-29T03:55:02Z","actor":"bob-cli-dm.7.1.3","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-dm.7.1.3","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Successor picker now carries per-row task context {path, one-based line, full note text, displayText, status, preimage} through NAV's model normalizer and the cycler picker model. Ctrl+Shift+Enter retargets one highlighted row or marked rows sequentially in displayed order, each pick getting that task's refreshed context; choices publish only after every pick succeeds. Cancel, changed/missing source, or closing the successor modal while awaiting leaves previous overrides, marks, and selection unchanged. Validated themeIntent {deliberate, linkOnce, shown} and preserveSpelling survive both NAV normalizeSuccessorDestinationOverride and cycler normalizeSuccessorPickDestination/normalizeSuccessorPicks; malformed intent is dropped without rejecting the destination; linkOnce overrides deliberate. Older rows and missing pickers still retarget without theme permission. Theme writes remain for 7.1.4.\n\nVerified: npm run build; node --test successor picker, cycler offers, wiring, polish, and successors suites; npm test 4168 pass / 0 fail; npm run validate; docs inventory check up to date. sase bead epic-symbols: no leftovers. task-status-cycler deployed via bob plugins sync --no-pull. bob-navigation-hotkeys deploy refused (provenance: uncommitted build from bob-cli_14 at c59819c); did not force. Obsidian desktop UI unverified. npm run docs:check glossary.md drift is clean-base (see PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP)."}}
